From 3ebe67ca4b3c94f4e658cf45850371316db5a21a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "T. Kurt Bond" <tkurtbond@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 13:29:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/48] Strings.Insert at a position past the end appends

Insert called Append(dest, source), its arguments the wrong way round:
source is a value parameter, so dest was left as it was. Oakwood:
"If pos = Length(dst), src is appended to dst."

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/runtime/Strings.Mod | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
index 715c99b5..f8c7c7c9 100644
--- a/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
+++ b/src/runtime/Strings.Mod
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@
 BEGIN
   n1 := Length(dest); n2 := Length(source);
   IF pos < 0 THEN pos := 0 END ;
-  IF pos > n1 THEN Append(dest, source); RETURN END ;
+  IF pos > n1 THEN Append(source, dest); RETURN END ;
   IF pos + n2 < LEN(dest) THEN  (*make room for source*)
     i := n1; (*move also 0X if it is there*)
     WHILE i >= pos DO
-- 
